sn1.39:3.1 starts: “Earlier I had only heard that the Dhamma
sn1.39:3.2 starts: Has been realized by the One with Vision;
sn1.41:5.1 starts: “Then in the end one leaves the body
sn1.41:5.2 starts: Along with one’s possessions.
sn1.44:1.1 starts: A devatā:
sn1.44:1.2 starts: With its one root, two whirlpools,
sn1.44:1.3 starts: Three stains, five extensions,
sn1.44:1.4 starts: An ocean with twelve eddies.”
sn1.46:4.1 starts: “One who has such a vehicle—
sn1.46:4.2 starts: Whether a woman or a man—
sn1.46:4.3 starts: Has, by means of this vehicle,
sn1.46:4.4 starts: Drawn close to Nibbāna.”
